# Managed by the website repo (ops/caddy/form-limits.caddy, #124). ops/caddy-limits.sh copies
# it to /etc/caddy and imports it into each site block that serves the app. Change it in the
# repo, not on the server.
#
# Caps the request body on the public form endpoints, so an oversized POST is cut off at Caddy
# (413) after 256 KB instead of being read in full by Node. That covers the REST endpoint and
# GraphQL, where form submissions can also be created. The app's own limit on a submission is
# about 20,000 characters (src/hooks/limitSubmissionSize.ts), at most about 80 KB of JSON even
# in a script that takes several bytes per character, so 256KB never blocks a real message.
@sprecherEastFormSubmissions path /api/form-submissions /api/form-submissions/* /api/graphql /api/graphql/*
request_body @sprecherEastFormSubmissions {
	max_size 256KB
}
